  "source": "Entes EPM-04CS / EPM-06CS Modbus register table (A4263 Rev.2)",
  "notes": [
    "Entes EPM-04CS and EPM-06CS, rebuilt from the manufacturer's register table: several addresses of the previous map (minimum and maximum values, demand, voltage transformer ratio, connection selection and the alarm block) were wrong.",
    "Voltages are in 0.1 V, currents in 0.001 A, cos phi in 0.001, frequency in 0.01 Hz; the ranges in the table are multiples of the voltage (UT) and current (CT) transformer ratios.",
    "The table spaces its addresses by 2 and gives the format as unsigned int / int / short-int without a width; the map reads each as a 16-bit register.",
    "Warning levels and times of the alarm block are shown as plain integers (units as printed in the table). Some alarm rows of the table were hard to read; tripping times are listed in the same order as the releasing times.",
    "Not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
